 "notes": "Printed p. 297, cols 188-203; last leaf of Table XV Part II in the assigned range. Blocks: Mother-tongue Telugu concld. (cols 188-191: subsidiary Saurashtri, Tamil; earlier columns on leaf 302), Mother-tongue Tulu complete (cols 192-203: total returning; subsidiary Hindustani, Kanarese, Malayalam, Tamil, Telugu). Only Males/Females printed; persons null; where one sex is nil the other field is null. Layout: in cols 200-203 (Tulu/Tamil, Tulu/Telugu) the figures are printed noticeably lower than their row labels (roughly half to one line); rows were assigned by counting the nil-dot slots within each block of five rows and cross-checking against the Tulu total-returning column (e.g. the Kistna 2 males = Tamil 1 + Telugu 1; Guntur females 11 = Telugu 11; the '8 8 2 1' line cannot be Chingleput whose total is 1/1, so it is Madras). Two placements rest on slot counting alone and are consistent with totals either way: Tulu/Telugu 10/10 assigned to Ramnad (not Tinnevelly) and Tulu/Telugu female 1 assigned to Tanjore (not Trichinopoly). South Kanara Tulu/Malayalam females printed faintly ('2,4?0'); 2,460 is confirmed by the column total 2,797. All area totals reconcile."
